values ('e6f7a8b9-1c2d-4e56-9f56-6a7b8c9d0e66', 'social-work-ethics', 'Social Work Ethics', 'Social Work Ethics prepares students to identify, analyze, document, and respond to ethical issues in professional social work practice. Students study the NASW Code of Ethics, ethical principles, decision-making models, confidentiality, informed consent, boundaries, dual relationships, self-disclosure, professional competence, documentation, risk management, digital practice, research ethics, policy advocacy, and justice-centered practice. The course is case-driven and practice-centered. Students repeatedly apply standards to realistic dilemmas, consult across roles, write defensible documentation, examine power and oppression, and build a reflective professional identity capable of handling ambiguity without abandoning social work values.');

